# HakiOS fragment: the OPPO Reno Ace (pclm10) -- what is true of this device and of no other.
# Build inclusion, runtime defaults and installed cold-boot delivery are separate.
# Current user-facing checklist: notes/功能与交付状态.md. Compiled probes are not daily-use features.
CONFIG_DEVICE="pclm10"
CONFIG_HAKIOS_ADSP=y
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SPEAKER is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_MIC is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_BT is not set
# this phone's own Bluetooth half: the WCN3990's H4 link on QUPv3 engine 3 (0xc8c000), the
# three RPMh rails and the power-on pulse. wcnbt=1 reads the controller's versions, wcnbt=2
# also sends HCI Reset, wcnbt=3 downloads the TLV patch and NVM from /fw, wcnbt=4 the patch
# alone. Patched NVM baud at 115200 now responds; scanning/pairing remain unverified. Not in boot
# arguments until scanning works (devices/pclm10/drivers/bluetooth/hakios.wcnbt.c).
CONFIG_HAKIOS_WCNBT=y
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_CAMERA is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_TORCH is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOCINFO is not set
CONFIG_HAKIOS_ADRENO=y
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_HAPTIC is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_GOODIX is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_BUTTONS is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_QMI is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_MODEM is not set
CONFIG_HAKIOS_BATTERY=y
# The actual motor is AW8697, compiled with HAPC but controlled by aw8697=.
# PM8150B HAPC is not wired to that motor. PM8150L flash= controls are also test-only;
# neither physical success has yet been integrated into the normal iOS UI.
CONFIG_HAKIOS_FLASH=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_HAPC=y
# the processor and its clock are the sm8150 family's facts and live in soc/configs/sm8150.config:
# seven cores for the kernel, the top row of each group's own frequency table, and the memory vote.
# What is this phone's own is only where its firmware left the command database (cmdb= below).
# TSENS reads all 28 sensors in tests; threshold stop is not claimed as physically exercised.
# tools/pclm10-interactive.sh explicitly requests monitoring and thermal_stop=60.
CONFIG_HAKIOS_THERMAL=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_PMIC=y
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_BATTGUARD is not set
CONFIG_HAKIOS_SMB5=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_PON=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_BQ27541=y
# WLED is retained as an existing probe/default, NOT a verified retail panel brightness path.
# The lit panel is inherited from boot firmware; see notes/remaining-hardware.md.
CONFIG_HAKIOS_WLED=y
# the keys were made to work here and were verified end to end on the phone: the kernel sees every
# press (logs/100547-run.log: volume down and volume up, with held times) and backboardd receives
# the iOS VolumeDecrement/VolumeIncrement usage codes. pon=1 is what switches the driver on.
# bq27541=1 reads the pack's gauge over the two bit-banged pins (devices/pclm10/drivers/power/
# hakios.bq27541.c); it still does not acknowledge. UI percent is a voltage estimate.
# cmdb=0x85f20000 is where this phone's firmware left the RPMh command database, which the clock
# driver reads to vote for memory bandwidth: its tree keeps only a pointer to it (qcom,cmd-db@c3f000c,
# which this phone's touch driver followed, logs/012447-run.log), and every round has found the same
# 4424-byte table at the same place. The reference phone's sits at a fixed address and needs nothing.
# smb5=1 belongs here too: the charger and the pack's voltage through the PMIC's own gauge were read
# on the phone (logs/113935-run.log: 4.31 V, and the charge the status line describes), and it is
# the SMB5 thread that asks the pack gauge again every five seconds -- without smb5=1 the bq27541
# probe never runs at all, which is why the 02:12 round showed no gauge lines.
# The S3706 report path was verified on this phone (logs/210849-run.log).
# Build AND enable it by default; compiling S3706 alone leaves touch off.
# fb_beam=0: the merged upstream kernel's default (1: rows written behind the panel's scan line) resets
# this phone within 150 s -- with it a 150 s run ends in a fresh loader; without it the run returns
# normally and SpringBoard comes up (logs/p2-merged-2026-11-05 vs logs/p2-fbeam0-2026-11-05). The
# write-behind-scan path is still to be fixed for pclm10; the argument stays here until then.
CONFIG_BOOTARGS="pon=1 bq27541=1 wled=1 smb5=1 cmdb=0x85f20000 touch=1 fb_beam=0"
CONFIG_HAKIOS_S3706=y
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_UFS is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_WIFI is not set
# the SLPI, the subsystem this phone's WLAN runs on: M1 of notes/wifi.md §5, its four rails
# voted through RPMh and its q6 block read once (devices/pclm10/drivers/wifi/hakios.slpi.c).
# Built to be brought up on the phone; slpi= is not in the boot arguments until the phone has
# answered, and the q6 read can end the run if the block does not answer unpowered.
CONFIG_HAKIOS_SLPI=y
# CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN is not set
# CONFIG_GPU is not set
# CONFIG_ADSP is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_WIFI is not set
# CONFIG_MODEM is not set
# CONFIG_MODEM_AGAIN is not set
# CONFIG_FIRMWARE is "device" in the common kernel: say "none" here until this device's firmware is pulled
